# Kotlin & Android Patterns

## Compose & UI
- Fragments extend **CoreFragment** and implement **ComposeView()**; use **CoreLayout** for topBar/bottomBar/content.
- Use **collectAsState()** for ViewModel state in Composables. Keep UI state in **XxxUiState** data classes.
- Use **stringResource(R.string.xxx)** for user-facing text.

## ViewModels & Data
- ViewModels get repositories via Koin **by viewModel()**; repositories use **Flow** and **Resource** for async data.
- Do not pass **Context** into domain or data layer. Use it only in UI or **ui/util** (e.g. UiErrorMapper, LocaleManager).

## API & Errors
- Repositories that call network use **safeApiCallFlow { api.xxx() }** and map DTOs to domain in the block.
- In UI/ViewModel, handle **Resource.Error** and show message via **throwable?.toUiMessage(context)** when Context is available.

## Dependency Injection
- Register new APIs in **NetworkModule**, repositories in **RepositoryModule**, ViewModels in **ViewModelModule**. **AppModule** includes all submodules.
